  "clustering_unit_rationale": "The paired analysis retains repeated events because a control can be matched to more than one signal. Duplicated appearances are therefore not independent observations. Two things are reported: (a) a deduplicated analysis in which each distinct ticker+event-day identity appears exactly once, removing reuse entirely; and (b) CR2 inference clustered on TICKER, which is the defensible unit here because every duplicated control identity, and every repeated event, is nested strictly within one ticker. Clustering on ticker is therefore weakly coarser than clustering on event identity and absorbs both the repeated-event and reused-control dependence, as well as any within-firm correlation across separate earnings dates."
